    - target: {fileID: 7525514981268352495, guid: 49795ea11dec30d458081ce2900655d3, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Materials.Array.data[0]
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 2100000, guid: 5a1fae3ea127ff74ba8914315ce612f6, type: 2}
    - target: {fileID: 7971643174840413009, guid: 49795ea11dec30d458081ce2900655d3, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "\n\n\n\n\nProject Number: SCP-5000\r\n\r\nProject Class: Keter\r\n\r\nProject
        Title: Labyrinth of Infinity\r\n\r\nSpecial Containment Procedures: SCP-5000
        is contained within Site-\u03A9, a containment facility designed with infinite
        spatial characteristics. The interior of the facility is structured as an
        ever-changing labyrinth to ensure that SCP-5000 cannot be escaped from. Site-\u03A9
        is equipped with advanced navigation systems and emergency response mechanisms
        to deal with anomalous activities within SCP-5000.\r\n\r\nDescription: SCP-5000
        is an anomalous space that manifests as an infinitely expanding and ever-changing
        laboratory and park area. Once entered, all exits become indistinguishable,
        trapping anyone inside. The space contains multiple laboratories, each housing
        different SCP entities. Over time, these entities awaken and begin to roam
        the park.\r\n\r\nAnomalous Properties of SCP-5000:\r\n\r\nInfinite Expansion:
        The interior space of SCP-5000 is infinitely large, with no discernible boundaries
        or exits.\r\nExtradimensional Breach: SCP-5000 appears to exist outside of
        regular space, not subject to the laws of physics.\r\nEntity Awakening: SCP
        entities contained within SCP-5000 gradually awaken and become active, with
        diverse behavior patterns and abilities, increasing the difficulty of containment.\r\nShifting
        Labyrinth: The labyrinth structure within SCP-5000 constantly changes, making
        it difficult for anyone inside to find a fixed path.\r\nContainment Measures:\r\n\r\nRegular
        Patrols: Security personnel from Site-\u03A9 must regularly patrol the interior
        of SCP-5000 to monitor the activities of SCP entities and prevent their escape.\r\nEntity
        Surveillance: All SCP entities contained within SCP-5000 are to be equipped
        with surveillance devices for real-time monitoring.\r\nEmergency Response:
        In the event of an SCP entity escaping its containment area, an emergency
        response team must be immediately deployed to re-contain the entity using
        appropriate means.\r\nResearch and Analysis: The research team at Site-\u03A9
        must continuously study the characteristics of SCP-5000 to find potential
        breakthroughs in containment or methods of escape.\r\nAddendum: SCP-5000
        was discovered accidentally during an exploration of an unknown anomalous
        space. Since its discovery, the SCP Foundation has been working to understand
        and control this phenomenon. Due to its infinite expansion, SCP-5000 is considered
